      "text": "To determine the value of \\( z \\), we need to understand the process of projection of a vector onto another vector. The projection of the vector \\(\\mathbf{v} = \\begin{pmatrix} 0 \\\\ 3 \\\\ z \\end{pmatrix}\\) onto the vector \\(\\mathbf{u} = \\begin{pmatrix} -3 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -1 \\end{pmatrix}\\) is given by:\n\n\\[\n\\text{proj}_{\\mathbf{u}} \\mathbf{v} = \\frac{\\mathbf{v} \\cdot \\mathbf{u}}{\\mathbf{u} \\cdot \\mathbf{u}} \\mathbf{u}\n\\]\n\nFirst, we calculate the dot product \\(\\mathbf{v} \\cdot \\mathbf{u}\\):\n\n\\[\n\\mathbf{v} \\cdot \\mathbf{u} = 0 \\cdot (-3) + 3 \\cdot 5 + z \\cdot (-1) = 15 - z\n\\]\n\nNext, we calculate the dot product \\(\\mathbf{u} \\cdot \\mathbf{u}\\):\n\n\\[\n\\mathbf{u} \\cdot \\mathbf{u} = (-3)^2 + 5^2 + (-1)^2 = 9 + 25 + 1 = 35\n\\]\n\nSubstituting these values into the projection formula, we get:\n\n\\[\n\\text{proj}_{\\mathbf{u}} \\mathbf{v} = \\frac{15 - z}{35} \\begin{pmatrix} -3 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -1 \\end{pmatrix}\n\\]\n\nWe are given that the projection is:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{12}{35} \\begin{pmatrix} -3 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -1 \\end{pmatrix}\n\\]\n\nThus, we can equate the two expressions for the projection:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{15 - z}{35} \\begin{pmatrix} -3 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -1 \\end{pmatrix} = \\frac{12}{35} \\begin{pmatrix} -3 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -1 \\end{pmatrix}\n\\]\n\nSince the vectors are equal, the scalars must be equal:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{15 - z}{35} = \\frac{12}{35}\n\\]\n\nBy canceling the denominators, we get:\n\n\\[\n15 - z = 12\n\\]\n\nSolving for \\( z \\):\n\n\\[\nz = 15 - 12 = 3\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the value of \\( z \\) is \\(\\boxed{3}\\).",
