      "text": "To find the value of \\( z \\), we need to use the formula for the projection of a vector \\(\\mathbf{a}\\) onto a vector \\(\\mathbf{b}\\):\n\n\\[\n\\text{proj}_{\\mathbf{b}} \\mathbf{a} = \\frac{\\mathbf{a} \\cdot \\mathbf{b}}{\\mathbf{b} \\cdot \\mathbf{b}} \\mathbf{b}\n\\]\n\nGiven:\n\\[\n\\mathbf{a} = \\begin{pmatrix} 0 \\\\ 3 \\\\ z \\end{pmatrix}, \\quad \\mathbf{b} = \\begin{pmatrix} -3 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -1 \\end{pmatrix}\n\\]\nand the projection is:\n\\[\n\\text{proj}_{\\mathbf{b}} \\mathbf{a} = \\frac{12}{35} \\begin{pmatrix} -3 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -1 \\end{pmatrix}\n\\]\n\nFirst, we need to compute the dot product \\(\\mathbf{a} \\cdot \\mathbf{b}\\):\n\n\\[\n\\mathbf{a} \\cdot \\mathbf{b} = 0 \\cdot (-3) + 3 \\cdot 5 + z \\cdot (-1) = 15 - z\n\\]\n\nNext, we compute the dot product \\(\\mathbf{b} \\cdot \\mathbf{b}\\):\n\n\\[\n\\mathbf{b} \\cdot \\mathbf{b} = (-3)^2 + 5^2 + (-1)^2 = 9 + 25 + 1 = 35\n\\]\n\nUsing the projection formula:\n\n\\[\n\\text{proj}_{\\mathbf{b}} \\mathbf{a} = \\frac{15 - z}{35} \\begin{pmatrix} -3 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -1 \\end{pmatrix}\n\\]\n\nWe are given that this projection equals:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{12}{35} \\begin{pmatrix} -3 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -1 \\end{pmatrix}\n\\]\n\nEquating the two expressions, we get:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{15 - z}{35} \\begin{pmatrix} -3 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -1 \\end{pmatrix} = \\frac{12}{35} \\begin{pmatrix} -3 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -1 \\end{pmatrix}\n\\]\n\nSince the vectors are equal, their corresponding components must be equal. Therefore, we equate the x-coordinates:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{15 - z}{35} \\cdot (-3) = \\frac{12}{35}\n\\]\n\nSolving for \\( z \\):\n\n\\[\n\\frac{15 - z}{35} \\cdot (-3) = \\frac{12}{35}\n\\]\n\nMultiply both sides by 35:\n\n\\[\n15 - z \\cdot (-3) = 12\n\\]\n\nSimplify:\n\n\\[\n15 + 3z = 12\n\\]\n\nSubtract 15 from both sides:\n\n\\[\n3z = 12 - 15\n\\]\n\n\\[\n3z = -3\n\\]\n\nDivide by 3:\n\n\\[\nz = -1\n\\]\n\nThus, the value of \\( z \\) is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{-1}\n\\]",
